## Value types

### Value type: INT

64-bit signed integer, e.g. an exit code.

### Value type: FLOAT

64-bit float, e.g. a ratio.

### Value type: STRING

Arbitrary text. Quotes keep exact bytes, lone `$var` evaluates, `\{{ ... }}` interpolates.
Shared heap: cloning bumps a refcount, never copies the bytes.

### Value type: BOOL

Boolean `true` or `false`.

### Value type: LIST

Ordered list of values. Shared heap: cloning bumps a refcount.
The `frozen` flag marks `CONST`-owned buffers: every in-place
mutation choke point (`as_list_mut`) refuses a frozen buffer, so
freezing is deep and permanent. Only [`Value::deep_freeze`]
sets it, on a freshly detached tree.

### Value type: MAP

String-keyed map of values. Shared heap: cloning bumps a refcount.
Freezing mirrors `ListValue`: `as_map_mut` refuses frozen
buffers and only [`Value::deep_freeze`] sets the flag.

### Value type: PATH

Workspace path, resolved against cwd and guarded against escape.

### Value type: DURATION

Positive time span: `500ms`, `10s`, `2m`, `1h`; bare number means seconds.

### Value type: PIPE

Runtime-managed stream handle, never a raw descriptor. A `PIPE` names a
runtime-managed byte stream with exactly one interface: declare it
(`LET $p: PIPE`), wire it (`WITH_IO`), and pass or copy it across
calls and module boundaries. Script code never manages descriptors,
temp files, or platform plumbing. The backend materializes lazily
on first binding (never eagerly at declaration), so the choice
always has full usage context. Cloning shares the backend
(explicit-sharing fan-out); equality is handle identity, never
byte comparison.

### Value type: HANDLE

Background task handle minted by `LET $t: HANDLE<T> = ASYNC ...`.
The payload names what `AWAIT` binds: `HANDLE<T>` yields `T` on
capture, `HANDLE<VOID>` is join-only (bare `AWAIT`/`CANCEL` only).
The handle itself is just a task id and carries no data: observe
the task through `AWAIT`, `CANCEL`, or `TASK_POLL`, never through
the handle. Copying it aliases the same task, and joining twice
fails. Bare `HANDLE` is not a declaration type: write the payload
or explicit `HANDLE<ANY>`.

### Value type: SEMAPHORE

Counting semaphore for admission control. Cloning shares the backend
(explicit-sharing fan-out); equality is handle identity, never the
count.

### Value type: PERMIT

Opaque admission permit minted by `SEMAPHORE_TRY_ACQUIRE`. Cloning
shares the release obligation (first drops release nothing, the last
releases once); equality is handle identity.


